{"id":23758,"date":"2020-01-26T11:46:17","date_gmt":"2020-01-26T11:46:17","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/?p=23758"},"modified":"2023-05-17T10:55:15","modified_gmt":"2023-05-17T09:55:15","slug":"the-best-windows-10-shortcut","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/the-best-windows-10-shortcut\/","title":{"rendered":"The Best Windows 10 shortcut Ever"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Windows 10 Creators Update, included what one of my colleagues called &#8216;a moment of zen at Microsoft&#8217;  \u2014 you can capture a specific region of your screen to the clipboard using the&nbsp;Win&nbsp;+&nbsp;Shift&nbsp;+&nbsp;S&nbsp;shortcut key. Having used it for a while I tend to agree with him. They call it &#8220;snip and sketch.&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To demonstrate how this baby works, I have selected a photograph from my Google Photos album and I want my photoshop expert to change a few things on it. So first I used the &#8216;snip and  sketch &#8216; tool (Win-Shift-s) to grab the photo quickly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-1024x573.png\" alt=\"the snip and sketch interface\" class=\"wp-image-23761 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/573;\" \/><figcaption>Drag a horizontal crop across the screen to select the part you need. In this case some of the photo.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-1.png\" alt=\"crop the chosen image\" class=\"wp-image-23762 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 679px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 679\/782;\" \/><figcaption>In doing so I can crop the image <\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In my notifications bar on the right of my screen, I can see the image has been saved to a universal clipboard. From here you can paste it in almost ANYWHERE with a cursor and a Ctrl_V. I haven&#8217;t found anywhere yet where it will not paste effectively.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-2.png\" alt=\"the notification toolbar\" class=\"wp-image-23763 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 788px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 788\/455;\" \/><figcaption>The notifications bar shows a clickable image<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Alternatively, if you want to edit it quickly just double click the notification and Windows will launch it in a basic editor application.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-3-1024x552.png\" alt=\"mark up on an image\" class=\"wp-image-23764 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/552;\" \/><figcaption>Make any edits or markups you want on the image. I&#8217;m showing our photoshop guru I want some burn-in on the areas ringed<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">then use the shortcut AGAIN to copy the image and paste it into an email or blog (as I have done).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-4.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-23765 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 810px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 810\/780;\" \/><figcaption>And paste it straight into a blog or email, Onenote page or even a blank canvas in Photoshop <\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-5-1024x708.png\" alt=\"the photo pasted into photoshop\" class=\"wp-image-23766 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/708;\" \/><figcaption>Pasted into Photoshop<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The beauty is, is that at no stage have I had to save or name or find the image. For me, that is a massive saving of time and effort.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The other part of my working day is within Excel, and here again, the shortcut can be hugely beneficial.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/01\/image-7.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-23771 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 391px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 391\/792;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The client has a problem with a particular value in their pivot table.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It&#8217;s an easy enough solution, the point is, that that single image so easily executed using snip and stretch then demonstrates so well the problem, and this can now be shared on <a href=\"https:\/\/www.whatsapp.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Whatsapp (opens in a new tab)\">Whatsapp<\/a>, email, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.skype.com\/en\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"skype (opens in a new tab)\">skype<\/a>&#8230; Sure you can use a screen share but so often an email or an SMS message suits you both fine.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"As a company director (opens in a new tab)\">As a company director<\/a>, communication is obviously key, and to do this, I must use the broadest range of communication channels possible.  This feature of windows helps us to help our customers, to help us, to help them.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I hope that you find this shortcut as useful as I have.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Windows 10 Creators Update, included what one of my colleagues called &#8216;a moment of zen at Microsoft&#8217; \u2014 you can capture a specific region of your screen to the clipboard using the&nbsp;Win&nbsp;+&nbsp;Shift&nbsp;+&nbsp;S&nbsp;shortcut key. Having used it for a while I tend to agree with him. They call it &#8220;snip and sketch.&#8221; To demonstrate how this<a class=\"excerpt-read-more\" href=\"https:\/\/www.theexcelexperts.com\/the-best-windows-10-shortcut\/\" title=\"ReadThe Best Windows 10 shortcut Ever\">&#8230; Read more &raquo;<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":23762,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"om_disable_all_campaigns":false,"_mo